Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.49,0:00:07.38,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,S-So, uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.38,0:00:10.52,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,We just gained a new friend today!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.52,0:00:12.89,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,This is Miss Lainie, \Ndaughter of Baron Cyan.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.89,0:00:14.35,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Be nice to her, everyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.94,0:00:21.16,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.61,0:00:26.02,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Oh, do forgive me. This calls for tea.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.02,0:00:27.58,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Please wait a moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.34,0:00:31.51,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Lainie...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.01,0:00:35.59,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I've been informed of your circumstances,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.59,0:00:39.91,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,and I have no feelings \Non the matter whatsoever.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.16,0:00:45.14,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But I'm sure it still weighs on your mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.14,0:00:48.93,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm not sure if I should \Ncondemn you or forgive you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.86,0:00:51.64,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It's too complicated.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.64,0:00:53.07,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.00,0:00:58.23,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Please, no! There's nothing \Nyou need to apologize for!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.23,0:01:00.03,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,It was all my fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.82,0:01:05.49,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Lainie, did you put me in that \Nsituation with malicious intentions?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.49,0:01:09.45,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,No, of course not! \NI never meant any such thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.45,0:01:14.66,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,In that case, I cannot hold you liable \Nfor the misfortune you were born with.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.91,0:01:21.03,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You came here for your own reasons,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.03,0:01:23.43,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,which left you in need of help, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.01,0:01:28.15,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Which means I cannot very well \Nslap away these hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.53,0:03:12.96,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2}The Magical Revolution
Dialogue: 1,0:03:04.53,0:03:12.96,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2\clip(m 116 13 l 113 58 331 59 328 30 310 58 116 56 120 14 238 18 218 44 192 6 357 14 332 43 331 5 535 5 525 55 473 55 492 25)}The {\c&H7A4AE4&}Mag{\c&HE38B59&}ical {\c&H7A4AE4&}Revol{\c&HE38B59&}ution
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.53,0:03:12.96,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\fs15\pos(320,56)\blur2}of the {\c&H7A4AE4&}Reincarnated Princess {\c&H140900&}and the {\c&HE38B59&}Genius Young Lady
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.98,0:03:17.54,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,So this is the girl I've heard about.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.85,0:03:20.52,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You have magicite in your heart, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.62,0:03:24.46,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Tilty, Lainie is very sensitive.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.46,0:03:26.19,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Try not to scare her.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.61,0:03:30.92,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I hear you've captivated \Nmany young noblemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.92,0:03:32.93,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,How did...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.36,0:03:36.28,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh? What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.17,0:03:40.99,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I see. If I hadn't been told in advance, \NI'd have been in trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.27,0:03:45.44,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Something made me feel \Nsorry for her just now.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.85,0:03:50.03,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, so even people with broken \Npersonalities are affected, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.32,0:03:53.04,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Your fascination power \Nreally is amazing, Lainie!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.04,0:03:56.01,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,No, uh, I really have no idea what...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.30,0:03:59.21,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,So you're just activating it instinctively.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.21,0:04:01.68,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,It seems like inherent magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.95,0:04:05.39,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Actually, I would bet...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.39,0:04:07.33,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,{\i1}that's{\i0} what it is, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.33,0:04:10.31,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Ah... You thought so too, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.01,0:04:14.77,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,There aren't many people \Nwith magicite inside them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.77,0:04:16.28,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,There's no doubt about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.92,0:04:19.69,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I'm going to go get that thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.79,0:04:29.00,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,What is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.57,0:04:30.72,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,A forbidden text.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.06,0:04:31.90,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,A forbidden text?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.72,0:04:35.37,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Um, what is a forbidden text?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.37,0:04:38.64,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,They contain records of dangerous \Nideas and techniques,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.64,0:04:40.83,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,so reading them is forbidden.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.83,0:04:43.05,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,What is something like that doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.05,0:04:46.14,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Miss Anis brought it here. \NI don't remember when.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.14,0:04:47.93,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.93,0:04:52.84,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Uh, yeah, well... \NLet's put that aside for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.20,0:04:58.15,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,This is a collection of research notes \Nleft by a magician long, long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.17,0:05:04.31,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,That magician's goal was the \Npursuit of the truth of magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.66,0:05:07.38,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,But the path he followed was endless.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.38,0:05:10.53,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,He would never reach its terminus, \Neven after spending his life on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.77,0:05:13.66,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,So the magician decided to make \Nup for his insufficient lifespan
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.66,0:05:15.99,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,by using the lives of others.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.51,0:05:19.20,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But... how?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.20,0:05:22.53,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,He used the power of magicite.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.97,0:05:26.19,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Not like my magic medicine...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.19,0:05:28.18,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,but much more directly.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.18,0:05:31.27,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,He embedded magicite that he'd \Nstolen directly into his own body
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.27,0:05:33.60,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,and turned into a monster himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.60,0:05:36.55,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,And then he absorbed other people's lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.91,0:05:40.21,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You ladies heard stories about it \Nwhen you were little, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.21,0:05:44.30,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Stories of one who tricked humans \Nto create more like him,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.30,0:05:47.31,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,who deceived people under \Nthe cover of night.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.31,0:05:50.21,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,The frightening monster \Nspoken of in fairy tales...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.75,0:05:52.08,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,The vampire.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.95,0:05:57.67,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Wait a moment. What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.02,0:06:01.88,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Were we not just discussing \Nthe issue concerning Miss Lainie?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.88,0:06:06.35,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,They say anyone whose blood is sucked \Nby a vampire becomes a vampire.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.77,0:06:11.06,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But according to that book, \Nit was actually a form of brainwashing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.06,0:06:12.69,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Brainwashing?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.02,0:06:18.66,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,In other words, the way a vampire \Nwould create more like him
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.66,0:06:21.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,was to overwrite people's \Nawareness to suit him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.47,0:06:24.44,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Our magician here had this thought:
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.44,0:06:28.12,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,If he were to create plenty of extras \Nwho would inherit his ideology,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.12,0:06:31.91,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,and if one of them should arrive at \Nthe truth one day, that would suffice.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.04,0:06:34.42,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,How vile.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.90,0:06:38.34,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,A human using the power of magicite \Nto manipulate people's thoughts...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.75,0:06:41.78,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,That's a story we've heard \Nsomewhere recently, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.78,0:06:45.68,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,You mean I'm... a vampire?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.96,0:06:53.93,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, well... maybe not so much a vampire, \Nbut the descendant of one?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.93,0:06:58.15,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,The forbidden text says magicite within \Na person's body becomes hereditary,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.15,0:07:02.89,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,so most likely, your mother's \Nmother's mother's... uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.89,0:07:06.64,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I mean, if you could learn \Nto control your own power,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.64,0:07:08.88,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,that would actually be amazing!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.88,0:07:10.56,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Would it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.56,0:07:14.18,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,That sounds interesting. Let's experimen—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.18,0:07:16.28,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I mean, start training you right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.55,0:07:19.26,Default,Title,0,0,0,,You want to control the \Nmagicite's power, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.91,0:07:25.87,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,The flow of mana within you has stagnated.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.87,0:07:28.18,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Try doing exactly as I tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.18,0:07:29.75,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,O-Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.92,0:07:41.89,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Okay. Not bad for your first time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.89,0:07:43.86,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,We'll stop here for today.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.86,0:07:45.65,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.37,0:07:48.60,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh? Lainie, your eyes...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.87,0:07:49.60,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.78,0:07:57.52,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,H-Huh? What is this? My teeth...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.52,0:07:58.00,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Your teeth?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.37,0:07:59.95,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Whoa! Fangs!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.95,0:08:01.77,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Well, Lainie?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.77,0:08:04.16,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Do you feel like you can keep \Nyour fascination power in check?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.45,0:08:05.87,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Oh... Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.87,0:08:08.90,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,It's as if a fog I had within me \Njust cleared up...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.90,0:08:13.13,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,I feel like I can clearly understand \Nhow to use my power now!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.13,0:08:16.15,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,The vampire magicite has been activated.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.15,0:08:17.60,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Just as I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.87,0:08:20.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Everything's up to you now, Lainie.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.47,0:08:24.85,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,In her case, having magicite within her body \Nhad become a matter of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.85,0:08:28.53,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Leaving it inactive within her \Nwas actually unhealthy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.53,0:08:31.77,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So now that the flow of mana \Nwithin you has been activated,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.55,0:08:32.52,DefaultTop,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Those two are incredible.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.77,0:08:34.49,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,you should be able to control it \Nat will from now on!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.90,0:08:37.99,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,It doesn't feel as if Lainie \Nis doing anything right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.99,0:08:39.39,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Which probably means...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.18,0:08:41.91,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie? Something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.91,0:08:44.13,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,No, nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.31,0:08:50.93,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Oh, right. I need to return \Nthis to the library.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.93,0:08:53.64,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,But I'd be bored going by myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.64,0:08:57.18,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Miss Anis, I'm going to borrow \NLady Euphyllia for a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.18,0:08:58.08,Default,Anisphia/Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.36,0:09:05.26,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.64,0:09:07.48,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,So?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.73,0:09:08.57,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.93,0:09:12.90,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You were giving me quite \Na serious look back there.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.23,0:09:15.73,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Is there something you'd like to say to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.18,0:09:17.86,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Uh, not particularly...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.97,0:09:20.26,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Are you jealous?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.78,0:09:26.76,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Wait, what's her deal? \NDoes she not even realize it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.76,0:09:28.75,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Is that how I looked?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.06,0:09:32.86,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I'd like to know what else \Nit could have looked like.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.89,0:09:35.42,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.90,0:09:38.94,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,So I was jealous.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.68,0:09:43.60,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Ugh, you're such a pain to deal with!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.42,0:09:46.80,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Just what are you to Miss Anis?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.46,0:09:49.78,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm... her assistant.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.78,0:09:53.52,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I'm asking if you really see \Nyourself as her assistant!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.63,0:09:59.03,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Oh, don't make that face at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.03,0:10:01.67,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You make it look like I'm the bad guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.20,0:10:05.08,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,The reason Miss Anis \Ntook you as her assistant
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.08,0:10:08.13,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,was to restore your lost honor, was it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.99,0:10:13.08,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,She achieved that goal when she defeated \Nthe dragon, and on top of that,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.08,0:10:16.58,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,she went on to solve the mystery \Nof Lainie and the strife she caused.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.04,0:10:20.54,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,So what reason do you have \Nto continue being her assistant?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.06,0:10:23.01,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.28,0:10:26.90,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,It's not as if I'm trying \Nto take away your role.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.90,0:10:32.26,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I help Miss Anis because I find her \Nmagicology and magic tools fascinating,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.26,0:10:37.61,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,but I have no intention of going along with \Nher foolish dream of becoming a magician.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.07,0:10:39.94,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.45,0:10:42.40,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Enough talking about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.40,0:10:45.05,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I'm asking about {\i1}you{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.05,0:10:47.36,Default,Euphie,0,0,0,,What... about me?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.36,0:10:51.30,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,For instance, when Prince Algard \Nbecomes the next king,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.30,0:10:56.84,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,he might exile Miss Anis to the remote \Nborderlands out of prejudice against her.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.30,0:10:59.56,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Would you be able to accompany her?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.80,0:11:05.78,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Of course. You can't give an immediate \Nanswer in the heat of the moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.78,0:11:10.56,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What you say and do steers the fate \Nof the Magenta family, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.10,0:11:14.37,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Miss Anis is a heretic.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.37,0:11:17.64,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,If you stand by her with half-hearted \Nintentions, you'll regret it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.88,0:11:19.92,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I suggest you give it some serious thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.83,0:11:24.31,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.47,0:11:35.66,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Come in.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.71,0:11:40.07,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.51,0:11:41.92,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Is something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.92,0:11:46.38,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh? Oh, I don't really need anything...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.63,0:11:50.61,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I just thought you seemed kind of down.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.47,0:11:58.56,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What were you up to, Euphie?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.32,0:12:01.03,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Well, I suppose...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.03,0:12:03.98,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I was thinking about the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.98,0:12:06.05,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What does that mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.05,0:12:09.26,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Now that things have started to calm down,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.26,0:12:10.78,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I was pondering what comes next.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.14,0:12:12.91,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.06,0:12:16.68,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I don't want to be half-hearted.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.76,0:12:19.37,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh? What'd you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.37,0:12:21.19,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Nothing at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.65,0:12:25.05,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I was...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.55,0:12:31.02,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I was just wondering what it is \NI really want to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.61,0:12:32.98,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Did you find your answer?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.29,0:12:38.70,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Why do you like magic so much?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.61,0:12:41.30,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well, that came out of nowhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.30,0:12:45.65,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Hmm... All I can really say \Nis because I like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.41,0:12:49.86,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's like being in love, I think. \NNot that I'd know.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.59,0:12:53.83,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I want to fall in love like that, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.52,0:13:00.77,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Hey, Euphie... Can I sleep in here tonight?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.51,0:13:14.10,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,U-Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.04,0:13:21.47,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Miss Lainie, is something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.88,0:13:25.21,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,W-Well... I just, um...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.70,0:13:27.34,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Can I...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.97,0:13:30.88,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,ask for your help again?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.15,0:13:35.29,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I don't mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.97,0:13:37.01,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Go ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.34,0:13:41.93,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,An impulse to drink blood?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.37,0:13:43.32,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.87,0:13:48.09,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well, we did activate \Nthe magicite inside her.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.09,0:13:51.66,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I think that makes her consume \Nmore mana than before.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.06,0:13:54.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And when her body feels low on mana,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.47,0:13:57.76,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,it manifests in the form of \Nan impulse to drink blood.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.76,0:13:59.56,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Leave it to a vampire.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.56,0:14:03.74,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,So she can take the mana from other \Npeople's blood and make it her own.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.74,0:14:06.12,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Have you let her drink any?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.12,0:14:07.83,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Yes, Ilia has.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.88,0:14:15.37,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,We offered ours, too, but she told us \Nto remember our positions.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.37,0:14:19.23,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,I am truly grateful to Miss Ilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.61,0:14:21.74,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Princess.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.52,0:14:23.86,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, Ilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.86,0:14:27.19,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Wait, what's wrong? Why the dark look?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.19,0:14:29.96,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I just received this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.49,0:14:32.27,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,It's from the Ministry of the Arcane.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.06,0:14:34.65,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Ugh...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.02,0:14:36.59,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What a pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.92,0:14:39.56,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What did that garbage ministry say?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.56,0:14:43.53,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,They want Miss Anis to give a lecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.76,0:14:46.49,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,A lecture? That's amazing, Miss Anis!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.01,0:14:49.43,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, it's not that kind of thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.72,0:14:53.07,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Basically, they want me to explain \Nin front of a bunch of people
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.07,0:14:55.40,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,what I plan to do with the \Nmaterials from the dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.70,0:14:57.36,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.96,0:15:04.53,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,This is quite an aggressive letter.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.86,0:15:06.75,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Right? Who wants anything to do with that?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.75,0:15:08.83,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,U-Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.83,0:15:12.46,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,The elites in the Ministry of \Nthe Arcane value tradition.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.46,0:15:15.73,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,They're not fond of the princess's \Nmagicology and magic tools.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.97,0:15:18.51,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,They say it's not in line \Nwith belief in the spirits,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.51,0:15:20.95,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,and that it'll be a negative \Ninfluence on the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.95,0:15:26.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,They just want to find fault with me \Nand take all my materials again.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.44,0:15:29.39,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,So what are you going to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.39,0:15:31.91,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,If you refuse to do the lecture \Nbecause it's a hassle,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.91,0:15:36.56,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,it'll just raise undue suspicions \Nand lead to more nasty rumors.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.12,0:15:38.98,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,And it won't just be you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.98,0:15:41.83,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,All those close to you will suffer for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.22,0:15:43.64,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I don't want that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.28,0:15:45.29,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That said, though...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.78,0:15:49.46,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What should I do? \NThat dragon's materials are valuable.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.46,0:15:52.19,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I don't want to lose a single one of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.70,0:15:56.54,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Okay! I'll just have to come up \Nwith a new product
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.54,0:15:59.14,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,that'll convince even \Nthe Ministry of the Arcane!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.41,0:16:05.46,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Would those people be convinced \Nby anything a heretic princess says?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.46,0:16:06.52,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Good point.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.80,0:16:10.03,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Ugh, damn that Ministry of the Arcane!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.43,0:16:11.79,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.03,0:16:15.44,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Could you leave this matter to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.44,0:16:16.10,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.00,0:16:41.86,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Greetings, ladies and gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.86,0:16:45.57,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I am Anisphia Wynn Palettia, \Nyour speaker for today.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.13,0:16:50.75,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Oh, dear. Not a very receptive crowd.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.04,0:16:52.44,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,No kidding.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.29,0:16:57.90,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I will now give my presentation \Nexplaining how I intend
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.90,0:17:00.36,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,to use the materials \Nfrom the dragon I defeated.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.90,0:17:01.84,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.18,0:17:06.29,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Before I get started, I'd like you \Nto take a look at this magic tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.56,0:17:10.00,Default,Ministry Official A,0,0,0,,A magic tool? Part of that shady \Nbusiness you call "magicology"?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.00,0:17:14.22,Default,Ministry Official B,0,0,0,,Isn't mimicry of magic \Nsacrilege against the spirits?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.49,0:17:16.18,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,This is my Witch's Broom,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.47,0:17:20.38,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,a tool of flight that I invented \Nusing magicology.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.76,0:17:25.61,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Using this, we can venture into the \Nunexplored territory we know as the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.61,0:17:30.57,Default,Ministry Official C,0,0,0,,Who would use such a thing other \Nthan the mad princess? Ridiculous!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.57,0:17:34.52,Default,Ministry Official D,0,0,0,,A princess who can't even use magic \Nis truly unworthy of our time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.45,0:17:36.48,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Wow...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.06,0:17:40.45,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,These old geezers aren't going to do \Nanything but find fault with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.82,0:17:41.91,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.19,0:17:51.08,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I am Princess Anisphia's assistant,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.42,0:17:53.29,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Euphyllia Magenta.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.58,0:17:59.26,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,From this point onward, I will interject \Nmy own opinions as a magician.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.55,0:18:02.21,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,The genius daughter of Duke Magenta?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.49,0:18:06.49,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,As you all know,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.49,0:18:10.22,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,the power of flight is exceedingly \Ndifficult to both acquire and master.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.22,0:18:14.85,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It has long been accepted that \Nnot just anyone can freely fly.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.26,0:18:18.67,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But magic tools of flight make that possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.06,0:18:23.62,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I say this as one who has seen \NHer Highness's research up close.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.62,0:18:25.89,Default,NobleA,0,0,0,,Anyone can fly, eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.89,0:18:28.84,Default,NobleB,0,0,0,,Hmm, how very intriguing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.84,0:18:33.80,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,This Witch's Broom has already been put \Nto practical use by its inventor.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.16,0:18:35.31,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.08,0:18:38.39,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,This shape is unacceptable.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.39,0:18:40.73,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It seems to reflect its inventor's tastes,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.73,0:18:43.23,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,but it is problematic \Nfrom a safety perspective.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.23,0:18:47.33,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What? But brooms are what\Nwitches are supposed to fly on.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.33,0:18:49.16,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Where is that "normal"?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.16,0:18:54.62,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Therefore, Her Highness set out \Nto develop a more versatile magic tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.58,0:18:57.06,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Please take a look at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.33,0:19:00.98,Default,NobleA,0,0,0,,What is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.98,0:19:05.69,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,She calls it the "Airdra," representing \Nthe concept of flying like a dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.02,0:19:10.06,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,With this, the pilot's body is as stable \Nas if they were riding a horse,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.06,0:19:13.41,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,making it completely maneuverable and safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.85,0:19:16.71,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,If her research progresses \Nto the point of mass production,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.71,0:19:19.64,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,our kingdom's transportation network \Nwill advance by leaps and bounds,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.07,0:19:24.23,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,bringing with it the potential \Nfor immense economic growth.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.23,0:19:26.18,Default,NobleA,0,0,0,,If that's the case...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.18,0:19:27.85,Default,NobleB,0,0,0,,We can't disregard this research.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.30,0:19:31.54,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,In order to produce the Airdra,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.54,0:19:34.07,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,the materials from the \Ndragon are indispensable.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.31,0:19:35.76,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Well, obviously.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.53,0:19:36.98,DefaultTop,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,The Airdra's unique structure {eadora no tokui na kouzou wa}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.76,0:19:40.53,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You came up with this tool specifically to \Nstop the dragon materials from being taken.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.98,0:19:40.53,DefaultTop,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,was inspired by the inherent \Nmagic that dragons use {doragon ga sono ... ukaseru tame ni mochiiru}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.53,0:19:43.71,DefaultTop,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,to keep their enormous bodies airborne. {tokushu na koyuu ... eta mono desu}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.79,0:19:42.56,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Shut up, Tilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.71,0:19:45.99,DefaultTop,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,And as you all know, {mata minasama goshouchi no toori}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.99,0:19:51.14,DefaultTop,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,different parts of a dragon act as catalysts \Nfor different types of magic, {doragon no ... narieru mono desu kara}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.06,0:19:52.16,Default,Ministry Official A,0,0,0,,It does make sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.14,0:19:55.20,DefaultTop,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,so each of those materials \Nplays a part in guaranteeing
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.09,0:19:57.83,Default,Ministry Official B,0,0,0,,But in the face of the \Nancient faith in the spirits...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.20,0:19:57.36,DefaultTop,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,the speed and safety of \Neach part of the Airdra. {izure mo eadora kakubu ... kitai sarete orimasu}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.07,0:20:02.93,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,This concludes my explanation of the \Nintended use of the dragon's materials.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.04,0:20:05.95,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,That wasn't too bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.95,0:20:08.35,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah. That's my Euphie.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.35,0:20:09.37,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.13,0:20:14.30,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I fear that the Ministry \Nof the Arcane may view
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.30,0:20:19.50,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,such revolutionary research as sacrilege \Nto the spirits and the gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.50,0:20:21.44,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Wh-What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.44,0:20:23.91,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,It absolutely {\i1}is{\i0} sacrilege!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.91,0:20:24.92,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.92,0:20:27.36,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Wow, you're pushing that far?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.36,0:20:29.32,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,No, I didn't ask her to!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.64,0:20:31.55,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Oh, this was her own decision?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.55,0:20:33.54,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Quite the assistant you've got there.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.62,0:20:40.14,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Knowledge of the world, \Nof reason, and of magic—
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.14,0:20:43.71,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,from a combination of these, \Nmagicology is born.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.71,0:20:45.84,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It is a field of study,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.84,0:20:49.42,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,not a practice intended to show \Ndisrespect to faith or tradition.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.90,0:20:52.09,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It is true that the Her Highness's magicology
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.09,0:20:58.89,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,is a bold concept unlike any presently known \Nto us, and may appear incomprehensible.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.89,0:21:02.86,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But that is simply an expression \Nof respect toward the spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.65,0:21:11.49,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,No, in fact, it came to be only \N{\i1}because{\i0} of that faith and tradition.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.22,0:21:17.76,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It is not due to a lack of talent \Nthat Her Highness
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.76,0:21:20.04,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,did not receive the spirits' blessing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.04,0:21:24.22,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It is because the spirits \Nrecognized the talents she has.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.22,0:21:26.89,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,That is what I want you all to understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.89,0:21:27.88,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.88,0:21:33.60,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I believe that now is the time \Nfor us to walk in step with change.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.96,0:21:36.57,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I would like all of us to strive \Nfor the future together,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.57,0:21:39.82,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,along with the foundations \Nwith which we have come this far.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.72,0:21:46.45,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,My only wish is that today will be the \Nfirst step toward that wonderful future.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.91,0:22:02.06,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Thank you, Euphie.
